      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: If an `if` block contains multiple attributes with different orders (e.g., `sources` and `deps`), this returns `std::nullopt`. Consequently, `assign_in_block` will skip over this `if` block when looking for an insertion point, defaulting to placing the new assignment at the end of the block.\n\nThis means that if we try to add `visibility` (which should be at the top), it will be placed at the very end of the target just because an `if` block happened to contain both `sources` and `deps`.\n\nConsider returning the minimum order found inside the conditional instead of `std::nullopt`. This ensures that attributes that logically belong before the conditional are correctly placed above it.\n\n```cpp\n    std::optional\u003cint\u003e result \u003d std::nullopt;\n    for (const auto\u0026 order : orders) {\n      if (order) {\n        if (!result || *order \u003c *result) {\n          result \u003d order;\n        }\n      }\n    }\n```",
